  "uncertainty_assessment": {
    "status": "NOT_CALIBRATED",
    "prediction_intervals_produced": false,
    "mathematical_requirement": "Under standard split-conformal prediction at a nominal 90% confidence level (alpha = 0.10), the required calibration group count n must satisfy ceil((n+1)*0.9)/n <= 1, which requires at least n >= 9 independent calibration runs per stratum.",
    "scientific_validity_distinction": "Meeting this mathematical floor of 9 runs is a necessary condition for computing empirical quantiles, but does NOT by itself guarantee reliable or valid prediction intervals. Scientifically defensible calibration in physical tribology requires verified specimen independence (specimen serial numbers, distinct material batches), exchangeability across environmental and testing conditions, tow-type-specific variance modeling, and separate empirical coverage validation on unseen runs.",
    "reason": "With only 7 training and 3 held-out labelled runs total, unverified specimen independence, and strong sequential ramp autocorrelation, prediction intervals cannot be defensibly calibrated and remain unavailable."
